WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
Republican Congressman

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.069
George Santos of New York is now facing

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.604
criminal charges.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:05.672
Sources telling CNN's

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.440
Evan Perez that federal prosecutors

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.441
have filed charges

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.776
against the New York freshman

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.810
and serial liar.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.479
He's expected to appear in court

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.346
as soon as tomorrow.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.514
Let's bring in Evan Perez,

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.648
who's breaking the story for us.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.616
Evan, tell us more.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:16.950
What do we know

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.551
about the charges specifically?

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.552
Well, Jake, right now

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.353
we do not know

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.888
the exact nature of these charges.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.490
We know that these have been filed

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.958
under seal

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.226
with the federal court

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.628
in the Eastern District of New York.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.996
That's, of course, the court

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:32.432
that has jurisdiction over

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.933
representative sentences district,

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.136
which is in Queens, in Long Island.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:37.670
We know that

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:38.405
at this point

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:41.408
he's expected to appear in federal court

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:43.143
to answer these charges

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.211
in Islip tomorrow.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.047
That's as soon as tomorrow

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:49.382
in an eastern district of New York.

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.851
Now, again, we don't know the charges.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.686
We know that the Justice Department,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.487
public integrity

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.289
prosecutors, the FBI,

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.223
of course, prosecutors

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.591
there in in the U.S.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.893
Attorney's office in Brooklyn

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.695
have been investigating the congressman

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.130
for a number of allegations,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.599
including charges or claims, rather,

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:09.469
that he falsified some of his campaign

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:10.870
finance filings.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.839
And so those are among

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.741
the things that we expect.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:15.708
Prosecutors

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:18.011
may be able to shed some more light on

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.512
when we see these charges

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.181
finally announced tomorrow.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.216
Now, this is a congressman,

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:23.983
obviously, Jake,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.784
that you've talked

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:27.053
about many, many times on this program.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.922
He took office just in January.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.024
And in just just a few months, of course,

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.992
it's come to light a number,

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.494
just a stunning number

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:37.597
of falsehoods and lies that he's told

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.698
as part of his campaign

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.033
in the lead up to this campaign

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.701
and in the years prior.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.269
I'll just recite just a few of them,

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.771
including his claim

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.505
on his resume

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.473
that he worked

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.541
at Goldman Sachs and Citibank.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.743
He said that he played

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.812
he was a star volleyball player

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:53.880
for Baruch College,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.748
which is where he said he got a degree.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.650
None of those things were true.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.751
He claimed, obviously,

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.954
that also that he had Jewish heritage.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.255
Something, again,

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.290
that has been shown to be false.

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:05.692
And, you know,

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.060
the congressman has repeatedly said

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.561
that he is not a criminal,

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.498
that he's not been charged with anything.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:12.765
We do know, though,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.500
in recent weeks

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.801
that he did admit

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.036
to a fraud charge in Brazil.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.738
Some number of years ago, Jake.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.039
And Leslie Jones once

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.975
said on The Daily Show,

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.643
Do you know how much you have to lie

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.511
to be known

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.779
as the lying congressman,

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.515
which says something, but of course,

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:29.249
lying to

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.317
the public is not necessarily

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.052
against the law.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.454
Some of the allegations

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:35.221
you've talking about

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.322
obviously aren't

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.624
including campaign

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.392
finance violations, potentially,

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.960
allegedly, and

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.595
fraud, stealing from that veteran

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:43.096
who had the sick

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:46.232
dog has Santos or his legal team,

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.367
if one exists

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.469
Responded to your reporting.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:52.639
We reached out to Jorge Sanchez's lawyer

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.673
this afternoon.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.008
He declined to comment, said

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.309
that he's not going to comment

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.744
on any of these allegations

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:59.712
until until he sees fit.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.447
We did see our Capitol Hill

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.883
team, Manu Raju and others saw him

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.685
walking the halls earlier today.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.920
He did not

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.488
tell us anything about what

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.556
his plans are for travel

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:10.690
to New York tomorrow.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.025
But again, that's where we expect

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:12.325
that he's

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.293
going to be able to

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.427
to answer these charges

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.296
for the first time Jake.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.331
In the Eastern District of New York.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.699
Let's bring in CNN's Manu Raju.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.935
Manu, Santa is also under investigation

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.102
on Capitol Hill

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.737
before the House Ethics Committee.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.139
But, of course, that's a rather

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.407
toothless organization.

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.675
Generally speaking, this

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:29.809
this seems more significant.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.645
Yeah, no question about it.

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:33.179
And also,

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.047
it will be interesting

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:34.480
to see

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.848
how Kevin McCarthy

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.317
the speaker, responds to this,

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.618
because for some time

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:41.154
he has now called on Jorge Santos

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:42.589
to resign, in large part

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.657
because if Santos were to resign,

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.358
this would open up

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.693
a special election

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:47.393
in a district

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.862
that Joe Biden carried in 20, 20,

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.464
something that could potentially flip

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.600
to the Democrats and narrow

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.500
Kevin McCarthy's

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.169
already razor thin majority,

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.870
which is why McCarthy for some time

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:58.204
has said,

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.173
let's let the investigations play out.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.174
He has pointed to the House

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.408
ethics investigation

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:02.942
as one

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.577
in which he will ultimately decide on

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:05.979
how to respond to Jorge Santos,

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:06.346
whether he would

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.680
call him to resign, saying,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.848
let's see what the House Ethics

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:10.016
Committee comes up with.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.351
We do know that the Ethics Committee

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:12.418
is pressing ahead

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.786
with this investigation.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.121
How long that

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.556
they they'll come to reach

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.590
any sort of conclusion

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.458
remains to be seen.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.893
But now that he has been indicted,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:21.928
Jorge Santos,

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:22.695
the question will be

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:23.529
whether that changed

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.498
the leadership calculation

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.066
or whether Kevin McCarthy

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.601
will come out and call

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.303
for Jorge Santos to resign.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.305
There are rules within the House

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.406
Republican Conference

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:34.440
that if for any member

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.608
who has been indicted,

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.110
they automatically lose

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.211
their committee assignments.

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:40.380
Recall, though, earlier this year, Santos

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.781
ultimately voluntarily

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:42.649
stepped down

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.183
from his committee assignments

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.185
after discussions with McCarthy.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.253
So whether there be

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:49.022
any other punitive measures remain

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:49.822
to be seen.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:50.657
Also uncertain

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:51.524
whether Santos will try

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:52.458
to fight this in court

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:53.226
or whether he will try

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.394
to run for reelection

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.763
He did announce just a few weeks ago

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.631
he planned to run for reelection,

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.900
despite the mounting opposition

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.002
from Republican leaders back home

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.238
and also many within his own conference

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.040
still said that he would try to fight

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.908
and try to win this electorally.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.810
Will that change his mindset

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.845
now that he has been indicted?

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.047
All big questions

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:16.282
but also a big question for the speaker.

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:17.917
What will he do about this

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.185
controversial member

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:20.386
who has now been indicted

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.721
within his conference?

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.423
Something that can narrow his majority.

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:24.791
If he were to step aside,

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.926
all big things that will certainly be

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:28.494
on the speaker's mind in Sanchez's

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.562
mind in the days ahead.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.064
Well, I think you answered your question

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:31.931
and in it.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:33.333
But I hear what you're saying.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:34.300
Let's bring in former

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.802
federal prosecutor Ali Hoenig.

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:37.570
How serious of a legal case

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.171
could this be?

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:40.106
Well, Jake, I guess

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:40.306
that will

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:40.807
be the big thing

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:41.808
that we find out tomorrow

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.209
when we take a look at this indictment.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.677
Important to understand

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.679
it is not a crime to lie to the public.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.314
It is not a crime to lie

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:49.482
about what you're going to do

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:50.316
when you get an office.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:51.250
It's not a crime to lie

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.051
about your background.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.252
What is a crime, however,

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.554
and what might be the case here,

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:55.455
we don't know

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:56.155
is the lie

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.223
in your Federal Election

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.624
Commission filing to lie

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.426
about your campaign expenditures.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.127
And you'll recall

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:02.562
there was reporting

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:04.597
that George Santos's campaign claimed

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:05.732
this whole series

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:08.868
of expenditures for $199

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:09.869
because the limit over

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:11.371
which you have to detail

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.606
those expenditures is $200.

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.708
I think that was awfully suspicious.

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:17.076
So I'd be looking for some sort

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:19.645
of official false statements charge here.

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:20.813
Again, we're speculating,

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:22.582
but based on what the public reporting is

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.017
CNN's chief legal analyst Lara

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.652
Koch is also joining us again.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:27.220
Laura, sorry,

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:27.754
I thought you

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:28.855
were going to get the hour off

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:30.289
after all of our Trump conversation.

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:32.191
But now we have another legal matter

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.426
dealing with a different

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:35.695
a different line New York politician.

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:38.865
How is this going to play out in court

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.733
when Santos appears as soon as tomorrow?

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.235
Obviously, one of the charges

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:43.669
but walk us through the choreography,

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:44.437
if you would,

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:47.206
Well, first, we're going to know

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:48.508
more about the actual charges.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:49.742
If it's sealed, of course,

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.677
if they're going to release the public

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:52.678
and what a judge would know

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:53.846
about an arraignment

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:54.647
and whether this is

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:56.649
going to be a multiple indictment

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:58.050
or one or more.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.418
Remember,

00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:01.587
you can oftentimes amend an indictment

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.790
to include more offenses later on.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.792
There might be conversations already

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:07.226
about the grand jury testimony

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:07.660
that came

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.395
in, if there was a grand jury impaneled

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:10.696
in this particular matter.

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:11.364
And we're going to learn

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:12.632
more about this, frankly,

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:14.801
likely as Jorge Santos does.

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:16.102
But as Ali articulated,

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:17.737
the nature of the charges

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:20.039
being the number of the charges

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:21.007
might not be known,

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:21.908
but certainly

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:24.377
the substance of what we know to be

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:26.379
the underlying cause for

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:27.780
the investigation is

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:28.981
has been quite clear.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:30.850
And if you follow the trail of money,

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.285
the idea of thinking about

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:35.054
whether transparency and accountability

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:37.023
can be actually served

00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:38.124
for the electorate,

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:39.125
that's going to be the key

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:40.460
for any campaign

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.662
finance or election related matter.

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:44.430
What was known,

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.332
what was relayed to the public?

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:47.500
And did the electorate

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.202
have a meaningful opportunity

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:50.369
to elect a candidate

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:52.472
of their choosing based on verifiable,

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:53.773
truthful information?

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:55.508
We take election related matters

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:57.210
very seriously in this country

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.611
because we want to have that level

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:00.680
of transparency and accountability

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:01.881
and the access

00:08:01.881 --> 00:08:03.983
to having someone you want an office

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:04.951
and remember.

00:08:04.951 --> 00:08:07.053
Speaker McCarthy was very reluctant

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:07.553
to say

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.555
what they would do about this seat,

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:10.356
trying to kick

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:12.325
the can down the road to suggest that

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:14.360
if there was a crime that occurred

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.761
then they would take action.

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:16.262
Well,

